@startuml adaptation-loop
title DeceptionGraph - what happens when a decoy fires

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName sans-serif

actor Attacker
participant "Decoy\n(lure + sensor)" as Decoy
participant EventBus as Bus
participant SecurityMediator as Mediator
participant ThreatProfiler as Profiler
participant AttackerState as State
participant AdaptationEngine as Adapt
participant IncidentManager as Incidents
participant PathPredictor as Predictor

Attacker -> Decoy : reads fake_production_database_password.txt
Decoy -> Bus : Event(DECOY_AUTHENTICATED, token)

Bus -> Profiler : on_event
Profiler -> State : next_state(event)
State --> Profiler : LATERAL_MOVEMENT
Bus -> Incidents : on_event -> opens INC-0001
Bus -> Adapt : on_event -> marks decoy BURNED

note right of Bus
  Observer fan-out: every observer
  hears the event, none of them
  know about each other
end note

Mediator -> Profiler : profile(actor)
Profiler -> Predictor : objective / next_hops
Predictor --> Profiler : db01
Profiler --> Mediator : stage, sophistication,\nobjective, next target

note right of Mediator
  The mediator owns the ordering:
  profile first, because everything
  else keys off the stage
end note

Mediator -> Adapt : adapt(profile)
Adapt -> Adapt : retire burned, then re-seed\nthat host with another family
Adapt -> Predictor : next_hops(current)
Predictor --> Adapt : ranked moves
Adapt --> Mediator : new decoys, one hop ahead

Mediator -> Incidents : apply_profile(profile)
Incidents --> Mediator : INC-0001 escalated to HIGH

Mediator --> Attacker : (nothing visible)
Mediator --> Decoy : Reaction\nprofile + incident + adaptation

@enduml
